      "website": "https://www.avoutcapital.com",
      "all_locations": "San Francisco, CA, USA",
      "long_description": "Avout provides non-dilutive financing to companies building in the physical world: robotics, space, drones, autonomy, and AI infrastructure & data.\r\n\r\nHardware companies need capital for equipment, inventory, and production long before revenue catches up. Today they fund it with venture equity, the most expensive money they'll ever raise, because banks don't understand the assets or move at startup speed.\r\n\r\nWe're starting with asset-backed lending and revenue-based financing, using a company's own operating data to make decisions quickly. Our vision is to become the financial rails for the machine economy.\r\n\r\nWe've done this before with real assets. Artem Milinchuk founded FarmTogether (YC W'18 accepted), a farmland investment platform he scaled to $220M in assets across 50 farms, and previously invested at Ontario Teachers' Pension Plan and was CFO at Full Harvest. Cofounder Cody DeVilliers built banking and payments infrastructure at Interac, Moneris, and TD Bank.",
      "one_liner": "Avout - new finance company for the American frontier",
      "team_size": 2,
      "highlight_black": false,
      "highlight_latinx": false,
